================================================================================
OBSERVATION
================================================================================
O-5  **Two near-identical `% …already…` messages on this platform mean OPPOSITE things**, and a
     future campaign will get this wrong without the distinction written down:
       `% DHCP Relay is already globally enabled`     (Group B, O-3) — an ADVISORY. The
             requested state HOLDS; the command was a no-op because it was already true.
       `% DHCP client is already running on this interface.`  (this case) — a genuine
             REJECTION. cfg.py exits 2 AND the configuration did NOT change; the client must be
             removed with `no ip address dhcp` before it can be re-specified.
     Both read as `% …already…` to a human skimming and as "error" to a stop-on-error driver.
     Only the second one actually leaves the device unconfigured, and only the first is a
     candidate for `console.ADVISORY`. Treating the second as an advisory would silently
     measure a default configuration and report it as the configured one.

