================================================================================
VERDICT: PASS -- the DHCP client's whole extended-identity surface on this build works as
configured and is observable on the wire: option 61 appears with the RFC 2132 type byte and the
interface MAC when `client-id` is set, option 12 carries the configured hostname, option 124
carries Allied Telesis enterprise number 207, and option 125 is added to the parameter request
list by `request vendor-identifying-specific` -- each absent in the baseline and each removed
cleanly by its no-form. No functional spec exists for "Extended ID", so the case was graded
against the TPS row, the X530 TPS grouping and the DUT's own enumerated CLI rather than a guess
at the title's intent. Two platform properties are recorded rather than graded: all SVIs share
one MAC, so `client-id <IFNAME>` cannot be discriminated by content (proven, STEP 2b); and
`% DHCP client is already running on this interface.` is a genuine rejection, not an advisory
(O-5).
